cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yangyi
title: "process-spine: Bayesian experimental design on measured process tables"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZhangYangyi03/process-spine"
abstract: >-
  A Gaussian-process surrogate and acquisition functions whose every objective
  evaluation is a row of a published high-throughput experiment table, so no
  simulator stands between the optimiser and the process. Benchmarked on 4599
  real amination experiments: expected improvement reaches 0.976 of the table's
  best within 64 experiments, against 0.939 for random and 0.978 for
  one-factor-at-a-time.
